{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/679394-aids-mary","id":679394,"title":"AIDS Mary","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-26T15:45:05-07:00","id":679394,"title":"AIDS Mary","content":"At the height of the HIV/AIDS scare in America, there was an urban legend circulating about a woman (sometimes a man but usually a woman) who would knowingly infect her sexual partners with the virus, often as a revenge scheme against whoever first infected her.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I was wondering if such a mythic personage might make for an interesting Slasher. They would most likely be an Avenger (if sticking to the narrative elements of the original legend), but I could see a case for Charmer too, or maybe even Genius.<br /> <br /> The primary problem I see with this idea is that HIV/AIDS doesn't guarantee death, especially nowadays with advanced medical treatments. And even when the disease is fatal, it can take a long time to kill someone, longer than most Slashers probably have patience for. Perhaps if the Slasher in question is a Scourge, their disease might be of a supernatural variety. Could even work as a new Undertaking: Plaguebearer or the like.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Has anyone done something similar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T15:54:39-07:00","id":679417,"title":"","content":"You're basically working on a Typhoid Mary situation. You'd definitely want a supernatural disease, but even a 'mundane' one could be super dangerous. Someone who happens to act as a carrier and isn't even suffering from the ravages disease can be good. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/GMhT0vI.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> There's a few supernatural diseases in the books, in Night Horrors: Wolfsbane, Versipellitis, which is more of a super STD. If you wanted it to be really nasty it could be a rage or zombie virus. The movie Contracted and its sequel are pretty good at showing this off. But that's a much more overt slasher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T16:20:13-07:00","id":679427,"title":"","content":"I presume the dividing line is whether they knowingly spread the disease? The original Typhoid Mary, Mary Mallon, didn't believe she was sick since she didn't show any symptoms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T16:45:49-07:00","id":679437,"title":"","content":"I haven't heard of an actual case of anyone doing that in America, but women have actually done that in other places. AIDS has about as much of a guarantee of death as any disease can have. HIV is less certain. As HIV is a virus it can mutate. A strain of HIV that is drug resistant and fast acting, leading to AIDS within a year, is possible. A supernatural disease would still be better since it would be easier to explain the Slasher not dying from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T17:01:25-07:00","id":679468,"title":"","content":"You could also go the mental route, with diseases and viruses in the form of memes and ear worms. Probably more likely for a Genius and Maniac modus operandi, if you add a supernatural element to it you can have things like Tao or <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1226681/\" target=\"_blank\">Pontypool </a>or <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KQ6zr6kCPj8\" target=\"_blank\">others</a>.<br /> <br /> It's an interesting idea, I'm sure it must come up somewhere in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-26-2015, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T18:47:41-07:00","id":679506,"title":"","content":"If you don't mind a little cross-over, a disease spreading Abmortal (from Geist: the SIn-Eaters) would fit perfectly. It would not only explain why they don't die from the disease, but why they are spreading it in the first place (namely, so as not to die).<br /> <br /> (You might design them as: they can't die as long as someone else is suffering from the disease. Since said victims will eventually die from it, it behooves the Abmortal to continue to spread the disease. To stop them, make sure there are no living infected running around.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-26-2015, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T19:01:57-07:00","id":679507,"title":"","content":"I had an idea about a Jim Jones-esque vampire who would gather large groups to him, perhaps enslaving them to the Vinculum, then encouraging everyone to commit suicide through drinking poison which he, of course, would be immune to. Leaving him free to go and do it over and over again.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be too hard to make it a human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T19:11:26-07:00","id":679545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/679394-aids-mary?p=679507#post679507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an idea about a Jim Jones-esque vampire who would gather large groups to him, perhaps enslaving them to the Vinculum, then encouraging everyone to commit suicide through drinking poison which he, of course, would be immune to. Leaving him free to go and do it over and over again.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be too hard to make it a human.</div> </div> </div> </div>SG-1 had an episode of similar ideas, based around the gou'auld Set. I recommend it to get a general idea for the hunter response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T00:35:32-07:00","id":679752,"title":"","content":"I remember an article about a man who was convicted for this, but he only managed to spread it to three victims before he was put away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/679394-aids-mary?p=679507#post679507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an idea about a Jim Jones-esque vampire who would gather large groups to him, perhaps enslaving them to the Vinculum, then encouraging everyone to commit suicide through drinking poison which he, of course, would be immune to. Leaving him free to go and do it over and over again.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be too hard to make it a human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of it being a vampire, and ending it by sharing a poison with the Ascending Ones that everyone except him is immune too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T08:25:34-07:00","id":685801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/679394-aids-mary?p=679427#post679427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume the dividing line is whether they knowingly spread the disease? The original Typhoid Mary, Mary Mallon, didn't believe she was sick since she didn't show any symptoms.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true. And most of the cases (in America anyway) of people infecting others with HIV/AIDS come from the carrier being either ignorant or in denial. I think there may have been one woman who was willingly spreading the disease to her partners, but it was nowhere near as widespread as the urban legend made the phenomenon out to be (whose moral is your standard &quot;don't have sex out of wedlock/strangers are bad&quot; type of thing).<br /> <br /> The disease would need to be intimate and fast-acting. Maybe a Vish Kanya type of situation.<br /> <br /> My primary hesitation at creating a new Undertaking to represent this is that no other Undertaking is so hard-coded to a particular M.O. Certain ones suggest particular trends, such as a Genius's predeliction for traps, but there's no, for example, throat-slitting Undertaking. Maybe it could work as a type of supernatural merit (or I could wait for Hurt Locker to come out and use the infected minor template). <br /> <br /> Now that I think about it, the legend could make for an interesting Beast character. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T08:45:28-07:00","id":685823,"title":"","content":"Did you know there was an attempt at a fan-splat focused on disease? It wasn't quite a titan like Princess or Leviathan, but it did post some interesting ideas and how these kinds of people might view themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T09:22:45-07:00","id":685848,"title":"","content":"Wasn't it called like Pathogen: The Infected or something? I recall some talk of it, but I never really looked into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T09:50:33-07:00","id":685861,"title":"","content":"Yep. The idea was a mixture of Resident Evil, The Thing, and various other body horror stories. The idea was that the disease, like all diseases, had an imperative to spread as though it was intelligent. Here, have a trope page.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/PathogenTheInfected\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...genTheInfected</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T10:16:39-07:00","id":685896,"title":"","content":"Well I'll just check it out th-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Paedomorphosis</i> - The Infected &quot;regresses&quot; in age and retains child-like behaviors. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T13:04:19-07:00","id":686089,"title":"","content":"...Hello? Did the line disconnect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T10:39:03-07:00","id":687269,"title":"","content":"I believe it's espritdecalmar's way of saying seeing 'Paedomorphosis' in a game left him speechless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T13:25:06-07:00","id":687430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/679394-aids-mary?p=687269#post687269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it's espritdecalmar's way of saying seeing 'Paedomorphosis' in a game left him speechless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give that the guy who created Pathogen has repeatedly gone on record saying that he regrets humouring one of his players by including that, I don't think that an unreasonable assumption. I've tried reworking Pathogen a couple times, but put it on hold to see how Deviant turns out, since I think it will do the same thing better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T10:30:17-07:00","id":688507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/679394-aids-mary?p=687269#post687269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it's espritdecalmar's way of saying seeing 'Paedomorphosis' in a game left him speechless.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit, yes. My apologies; I meant that post to come off as humorous but I think in retrospect it might have signaled as offensive instead. I'm sure the game is fine, that particular symptom just stopped me in my tracks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T10:51:38-07:00","id":688515,"title":"","content":"*Rimshot*<br /> <br /> Anyway, in terms of a slasher, I don't really know how much this undertaking moves into physical territory. If the hunters are going after this type of enemy, where's the danger to them? If they take proper precautions and go in with prevention in mind, the disease probably won't spread to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T11:21:43-07:00","id":688549,"title":"","content":"Flyboy's got a point. If this is a Slasher, and your party is supposed to hunt her (or him, let's be egalitarian here), the disease thing is pretty lackluster when it comes to threat.<br /> <br /> My recommendation? Use something more long term for the Plague. Make it some kind of mutagenic effect - zoonotic disease from Skinthieves, or a more infectious strain of Vespertilius, or a zombifying plague, maybe. Make the bulk of the Slasher's threat not the deaths she directly causes, but the horrible monsters she leaves in her wake. Because, really, there's not a whole lot that hunters can do to fight a plague - fighting plague-carrying monsters, and eventually the maniac who is creating them, is another story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T12:15:25-07:00","id":688576,"title":"","content":"This is true. I suppose while the Slasher might not be a direct threat, they might pose an indirect one, targeting the hunters' loved ones, rendering you paranoid about getting change from a vending machine or leaving your drink unattended. I imagine they'd make a good unseen antagonist, requiring hunters to spend some time connecting the dots. Maybe in the World of Darkness the CDC has a branch that works as a Compact or even Conspiracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T13:01:24-07:00","id":688659,"title":"","content":"I see that as a small and underfunded TFV cell based in Atlanta, reinforced by CDC or AMRIID doctors who find the truth, though I did write up a similar idea in Pathogen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T18:10:10-07:00","id":689065,"title":"","content":"More Hunter and less Slasher but the first thing that popped into my head was the short arch in the first Sookie Stackhouse novel about the dude who's boyfriend left him for a vamp so he intentionally gets himself infected with vampire AIDs and starts blooddolling himself out to anything without a pulse. Could make for an interesting Compact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/182-sciurrus","name":"sciurrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T01:31:40-07:00","id":689467,"title":"","content":"The disease as a weapon MO could actually fit the avenger/legend quite well, although I think a charmer or genius could use it as well. In fact, a genius manipulating sick people into spreading their disease would be particularly hard to track...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}